# Local-only values for `wrangler dev`.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (which is git-ignored) and fill in local,
# non-confidential values. Hyperdrive supplies the database connection during
# development, so no database credential belongs here. Never place production
# secrets or real client data in this file.

# ENVIRONMENT and RELEASE_VERSION come from wrangler.toml `[vars]`.
#
# Hyperdrive local development: `wrangler dev` needs a local Postgres
# connection string. The development binding in wrangler.toml defaults to
# `postgres://taxdesk:taxdesk@localhost:5432/taxdesk_development`. To use a
# different database (for example the managed development database), export:
#   CLOUDFLARE_HYPERDRIVE_LOCAL_CONNECTION_STRING_HYPERDRIVE=postgres://...
# An environment variable overrides `localConnectionString` without a file edit.
# The simplest place is a git-ignored `.env` at the repo root (copy
# `.env.example`); Wrangler auto-loads it before starting `pnpm dev:api`.
#
# Future provider credentials (for example OneDrive/Graph) are added here only
# with non-production test values when the corresponding story lands.
